  &lt;div class=&#34;ltr:hx-pl-3 ltr:hx-pr-2 rtl:hx-pr-3 rtl:hx-pl-2&#34;&gt;&lt;div class=&#34;hx-select-none hx-text-xl&#34; style=&#34;font-family: &#39;Apple Color Emoji&#39;, &#39;Segoe UI Emoji&#39;, &#39;Segoe UI Symbol&#39;;&#34;&gt;ℹ️&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

  &lt;div class=&#34;hx-w-full hx-min-w-0 hx-leading-7&#34;&gt;
    &lt;div class=&#34;hx-mt-6 hx-leading-7 first:hx-mt-0&#34;&gt;Originally published on &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.linkedin.com/posts/abhirockzz_agenticai-codingagents-opensource-share-7479589468312858624-PUiu/&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;&gt;LinkedIn&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
  &lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;No fluff, no hype: Kun Chen&amp;rsquo;s walkthrough is an all-hands-on-deck look at an agentic engineering workflow.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;It is also one of the rare public examples I&amp;rsquo;ve seen of how AI can amplify engineers who are already good at their craft. Kun walks through the environment and habits behind the results: terminal-based development, agent instructions and memory, skills, voice input, planning, validation, long-running tasks, and parallel agents.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=iQyg-KypKAA&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;&gt;&lt;img src=&#34;logo.jpg&#34; alt=&#34;L8 Principal’s Agentic Engineering Workflow by Kun Chen&#34; loading=&#34;lazy&#34; /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;I recommend watching the full walkthrough and subscribing to Kun&amp;rsquo;s channel. He also builds useful open-source tools; I&amp;rsquo;m already using and enjoying Lavish.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;blockquote&gt;
  &lt;p&gt;Learn more:&lt;/p&gt;
